From be873bd0a85408d9bbde1e8bae592aa872a431fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sankofa <sankofa@invalid>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:41:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] cronjob: translate the schedule by the scheduleSpread
 offset

With the feature gate enabled and spec.scheduleSpread set, every activation
of the schedule is delayed by FNV-1a-64(uid) mod maxDelaySeconds seconds.
A constant offset is a translation of the schedule, so missed-schedule
accounting, startingDeadlineSeconds, concurrencyPolicy, Job names and
lastScheduleTime all work on the translated times unchanged.

Signed-off-by: sankofa <sankofa@invalid>
Assisted-by: LLM
